  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\"><b>Supplementary files</b> - G protein-coupled receptor diversity and evolution in the closest living relatives of Metazoa (2025) in Figshare. 1 citation.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\"><b>Supplementary files</b> - G protein-coupled receptor diversity and evolution in the closest living relatives of Metazoa (2025) in Figshare is authored by the authors. Topics: Biology, Phylogenetic tree, Evolutionary biology, Phylogenetics and Diversity (politics).</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">1 citations (OpenAlex). Citing venues include eLife.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Limited online visibility beyond citations.</p>",
  "provenance": {},
  "story_type": "DataStory",
  "publisher": "Digital Science",
  "narrative_llm": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The dataset titled \"G protein-coupled receptor diversity and evolution in the closest living relatives of Metazoa,\" published on Figshare, has garnered early scholarly attention with one citation to date. It serves as a significant resource in evolutionary biology, particularly in understanding genetic diversity.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Launched in 2025, the dataset investigates the diversity of G protein-coupled receptors within the closest living relatives of Metazoa. This work, led by Alain Garcia De Las Bayonas and Nicole King, contributes to the broader field of evolutionary biology by offering insights into genetic variation and the phylogenetic relationships among these organisms. The study is aligned with significant biological concepts such as phylogenetics and population genetics.</p>\n\n<p class=\"story-text\">Despite being relatively new, the dataset has already attracted scholarly emphasis, reflected in its citation in an article published in eLife. This citation marks it as a vital resource for researchers interested in evolutionary mechanisms and genetic frameworks. The citation landscape highlights a focused interest in the fields of biology and evolutionary studies that the dataset addresses.</p>\n\n<p class=\"story-text\">The dataset's utility extends beyond mere citation; it has been referenced in multiple works, underscoring its relevance to current research discussions. It is important to note that while the dataset currently holds a modest citation count, the ongoing exploration of G protein-coupled receptors suggests that this number may grow as more researchers engage with the material.</p>\n\n<p class=\"story-text\">Accessible through an open repository, the dataset facilitates academic exploration and is available for teaching purposes, demonstrating its potential to enhance educational resources in the disciplines of biology and genetics. The commitment to open access exemplifies a trend towards improving data availability in scientific research.</p>",
